    - rid: 552786240694648889
      type: {class: StringEntry, ns: Unity.Localization, asm: UnityEngine.LocalizationRuntimeModule}
      data:
        m_KeyId: 1955544801361920
        m_Metadata:
          m_Items: []
        m_Value: Display World-Units as Improper Fractions
    - rid: 552786240694648897
      type: {class: StringEntry, ns: Unity.Localization, asm: UnityEngine.LocalizationRuntimeModule}
      data:
        m_KeyId: 1974903057825792
        m_Metadata:
          m_Items: []
        m_Value: Shows heights, positions and other distances as 1024ths alone (such as "6153/1024"), rather than as whole world units and 1024ths (such as "6 and 9/1024"). Either can be typed into a field, as can a bare number of 1024ths (such as "6153"), a decimal number of world units (such as "6.0087"), or a percentage of a world unit (such as "55%").
    - rid: 552786240694648898
      type: {class: StringEntry, ns: Unity.Localization, asm: UnityEngine.LocalizationRuntimeModule}
      data:
        m_KeyId: 1974903057825793
        m_Metadata:
          m_Items: []
        m_Value: Undo Steps
    - rid: 552786240694648899
      type: {class: StringEntry, ns: Unity.Localization, asm: UnityEngine.LocalizationRuntimeModule}
      data:
        m_KeyId: 1974903057825794
        m_Metadata:
          m_Items: []
        m_Value: How many changes can be undone, from 1 to 10,000 (50 by default). Each change kept takes memory (a change to much of the level takes more), so very high values can use a lot of it.
    - rid: 552786288315990065
      type: {class: StringEntry, ns: Unity.Localization, asm: UnityEngine.LocalizationRuntimeModule}
      data:
        m_KeyId: 2693706842521600
        m_Metadata:
          m_Items: []
        m_Value: Point Click Area
    - rid: 552786288315990066
      type: {class: StringEntry, ns: Unity.Localization, asm: UnityEngine.LocalizationRuntimeModule}
      data:
        m_KeyId: 2693706842521601
        m_Metadata:
          m_Items: []
        m_Value: How big the area that clicks a point (in Geometry mode) is, from the size it's drawn (100%) to twice that (200%). The point is drawn the same size either way.
